The selected checkpoint is from epoch 19. Its inference training NLL is 1.709206,
validation NLL 2.208655 and official-test-subset NLL 2.126871, with 26.5625% accuracy.
The falling training trace and variable validation trace show why the checkpoint is selected
on held-out NLL. Sixty-four test images do not support a comparison of architectures.

> Native confusion matrices

These matrices use the held-out predictions from the executed program above.
The native `ConfusionMatrix` SVG API labels exact counts with true classes
running from top to bottom and predicted classes from left to right.

\image(figures/alexnet_confusion_api_0.svg)
\caption(Held-out classification confusion counts, evaluation 1. Exact cell counts are printed in the image.)
\alttext(Integer prediction counts with true classes as rows and predicted classes as columns.)


> Conclusion

Grouped convolution restricts channel dependencies; LRN couples neighbouring channel energies;
dropout changes training evaluations while preserving deterministic inference. Exact geometry,
parameter counting, gradient checks and the small CIFAR-10 run test different claims. The subset
fit demonstrates the training workflow, not reproduction of the original ImageNet benchmark.

